    <desc>Copy, paste or open URLs, paths, hashes and more on the screen by typing a label.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Quick select</title>

<p>Quick select puts a label of one or two letters on every URL, file path,
  git hash, IP address, UUID and long number that the terminal shows, so that
  you can pick one without the mouse.</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press <keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Ctrl</key><key>Space</key></keyseq>.</p></item>
<item><p>Type the label of the text you want. This copies it to the clipboard. Type the label with <key>Shift</key> to paste the text into the terminal instead, or with <key>Ctrl</key> to open it.</p></item>
<item><p>Press <key>Esc</key> to stop without choosing.</p></item>
</steps>

  <section id="patterns">
    <title>Your own patterns</title>
    <p>To label other text too, such as ticket numbers, add Perl-compatible
    regular expressions with this command:</p>
    <code>gsettings set com.aripd.Pano.Legacy.Settings quick-select-patterns "['JIRA-[0-9]+']"</code>
    <p>Their matches are offered before the others.</p>
  </section>

